From: J P <1953637+jpwatters@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:35:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/54] Tab5 + relay: "Power on the radio" in the drawer
 (Remote Power-ON)

A QMX that is off has no USB device, so the Tab5 cannot reach it. The new
drawer row (Basic, under Radio source, section 59, N_DRAWER_SECTIONS 60)
asks the NAS relay to press the radio's power button through its FTDI cable
and opto board: "QMXR-PWR1" over UDP to the relay's port (7355, the same as
QMXR?), asked up to 3 times in 1.5 s on a short-lived task like Find NAS.

The relay answers "QMXR-PWR pressing", "on" (the QMX is on the USB bus),
"nocable" or "busy" (pressed in the last 20 s - asking again never becomes a
second press), and the Tab5 shows that as a toast. With the radio on USB the
row says only the NAS can switch it on. When the radio's USB device comes
back the relay opens it and the stream resumes on its own.

Firmware builds; check_drawer_sections, check_tx_guard and
check_unattended_tx are clean. Relay: nettest passes against the fake
radio, and the answers were checked with a stub power button. Not yet tested
with the cable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
